  "modules": [
    {
      "title": "Module 1 \u00b7 Central Tendency",
      "html": "<p><b>Mean</b>: $\\bar x = \\dfrac{\\sum fx}{\\sum f}$. <b>Median</b>: middle value when data is arranged in order. <b>Mode</b>: most frequent value.</p><h4>Key points</h4><ul><li>Mean $=7$. Deviations $|x-\\bar x|$: 1, 2, 3, 3, 5. Mean deviation $= \\dfrac{14}{5} = 2.8$.</li><li>Mean $=11$. Deviations $|x-\\bar x|$: 4, 8, 7, 4, 1. Mean deviation $= \\dfrac{24}{5} = 4.8$.</li></ul><h4>Worked example</h4><p><b>Q:</b> Find the mean deviation of 6, 9, 4, 4, 12.<br/><b>A:</b> 2.8</p><p><b>Q:</b> Find the mean deviation of 15, 19, 4, 7, 10.<br/><b>A:</b> 4.8</p>",
      "examples": [
        {
          "q": "Find the mean of 4, 8, 6, 10, 12.",
          "a": "$\\bar x = (4+8+6+10+12)/5 = 40/5 = 8$."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Module 2 \u00b7 Dispersion",
      "html": "<p><b>Range</b> = max \u2212 min. <b>Mean deviation</b> $=\\dfrac{\\sum|x-\\bar x|}{n}$. <b>Variance</b> $\\sigma^2 = \\dfrac{\\sum(x-\\bar x)^2}{n}$. <b>Standard deviation</b> $\\sigma = \\sqrt{\\sigma^2}$.</p><h4>Key points</h4><ul><li>Mean $=7$. Deviations $|x-\\bar x|$: 1, 2, 3, 3, 5. Mean deviation $= \\dfrac{14}{5} = 2.8$.</li><li>Mean $=11$. Deviations $|x-\\bar x|$: 4, 8, 7, 4, 1. Mean deviation $= \\dfrac{24}{5} = 4.8$.</li></ul><h4>Worked example</h4><p><b>Q:</b> Find the mean deviation of 6, 9, 4, 4, 12.<br/><b>A:</b> 2.8</p><p><b>Q:</b> Find the mean deviation of 15, 19, 4, 7, 10.<br/><b>A:</b> 4.8</p>",
      "examples": [
        {
          "q": "Find the range of 3, 7, 2, 9, 5.",
          "a": "Range $= 9 - 2 = 7$."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Module 3 \u00b7 Ogive & Quartiles",
      "html": "<p>An <b>ogive</b> plots cumulative frequency against upper class boundaries. From it we can read:</p><ul><li>Median at cumulative frequency $=\\tfrac{N}{2}$.</li><li>Lower quartile $Q_1$ at $\\tfrac{N}{4}$; upper quartile $Q_3$ at $\\tfrac{3N}{4}$.</li><li>The $p$-th percentile at $\\tfrac{pN}{100}$.</li></ul><p><b>Interquartile range</b> = $Q_3 - Q_1$.</p><h4>Key points</h4><ul><li>Median = value at cumulative frequency N/2.</li></ul><h4>Worked example</h4><p><b>Q:</b> On an ogive with total frequency $N$, the median is read off at a cumulative frequency of:<br/><b>A:</b> N/2</p><h4>More key points</h4><ul><li>On an ogive with total frequency $N$, the median is read off at a cumulative frequency of: \u2014 N/2.</li></ul>",
      "examples": [
        {
          "q": "If $Q_1=42$ and $Q_3=68$, find the interquartile range.",
          "a": "IQR $= 68-42 = 26$."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Measures of dispersion (range, mean deviation, variance, SD)",
      "html": "<p><b>Measures of dispersion (range, mean deviation, variance, SD)</b> is a key part of Statistics (Part II) (SSS 2, Mathematics). Master the meaning, the main points and how it is tested in JAMB and WAEC questions on this topic.</p><h4>Key points</h4><ul><li>Mean : $\\bar x = \\dfrac{\\sum fx}{\\sum f}$.</li><li>Median : middle value when data is arranged in order.</li><li>Deviations $|x-\\bar x|$: 1, 2, 3, 3, 5.</li><li>Mean deviation $= \\dfrac{14}{5} = 2.8$.</li><li>Deviations $|x-\\bar x|$: 4, 8, 7, 4, 1.</li></ul><h4>Worked example</h4><p><b>Q:</b> Find the mean deviation of 6, 9, 4, 4, 12.<br/><b>A:</b> 2.8 \u2014 Mean $=7$. Deviations $|x-\\bar x|$: 1, 2, 3, 3, 5. Mean deviation $= \\dfrac{14}{5} = 2.8$.</p><p><b>Q:</b> Find the mean deviation of 15, 19, 4, 7, 10.<br/><b>A:</b> 4.8 \u2014 Mean $=11$. Deviations $|x-\\bar x|$: 4, 8, 7, 4, 1. Mean deviation $= \\dfrac{24}{5} = 4.8$.</p>",
