      "html": "<p><b>Cumulative frequency curve (Ogive); median, quartiles, percentiles</b> is a key part of Statistics (Part II) (SSS 2, Mathematics). Master the meaning, the main points and how it is tested in JAMB and WAEC questions on this topic.</p><h4>Key points</h4><ul><li>Median : middle value when data is arranged in order.</li><li>An ogive plots cumulative frequency against upper class boundaries.</li><li>From it we can read: Median at cumulative frequency $=\\tfrac{N}{2}$.</li><li>Key points Median = value at cumulative frequency N/2.</li><li>Worked example Q: On an ogive with total frequency $N$, the median is read off at a cumulative frequency of: A: N/2</li></ul><h4>Worked example</h4><p><b>Q:</b> On an ogive with total frequency $N$, the median is read off at a cumulative frequency of:<br/><b>A:</b> N/2 \u2014 Median = value at cumulative frequency N/2.</p><p><b>Q:</b> The $p$-th percentile is read at cumulative frequency of:<br/><b>A:</b> pN/100 \u2014 The p-th percentile is at cumulative frequency pN/100.</p>",
